# Private application directory - never served over HTTP.
#
# These are the view templates the front controller renders; they are read from
# disk by PHP (App\Core\View), never requested by a browser. On their own they
# emit a fragment with no layout, no <head> and no security headers - and
# pages/admin/ renders the administration screens - so a direct hit returns
# partial markup that was never meant to leave the server.
#
# This directory was the one gap in the root .htaccess deny list: every other
# private directory was named there, pages/ was not, so under a document root
# set to the repository (htdocs/AI-UNIT symlinked one level too high) every
# template answered HTTP 200. It is now named in that rule as well.
#
# This duplicates the rewrite rule in the repository-root .htaccess on purpose.
# That rule needs mod_rewrite; this one does not, so the directory stays closed
# even on a server where the module is unavailable.
Require all denied
